Subject: [overlay 0018] Expose whether V_RenderView rendered the world this frame

V_FrameRendered(clear): true when V_RenderView reached R_RenderFrame this engine
frame. The visionOS immersive shell renders a second (right-eye) view by calling
V_RenderView directly; R_RenderFrame asserts without a registered world (boot, map
load, menus, console, cinematics), so the shell only performs the second-eye render
when the normal SCR path actually rendered the world, and shows the left image in
both eyes otherwise. The shell clears the flag at the start of each engine frame.
Applies after 0016 (independent hunks). Apply: patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro < this

--- a/src/client/view.c
+++ b/src/client/view.c
@@ -26,6 +26,20 @@
 int         gun_frame;
 qhandle_t   gun_model;
 
+// [stereo overlay] True when V_RenderView actually ran R_RenderFrame this engine frame.
+// The visionOS immersive shell consults this before its second (right-eye) render:
+// R_RenderFrame requires a registered world (or RDF_NOWORLDMODEL), so during boot, map
+// load, menus, console and cinematics a blind second-eye call would trip the world-cache
+// assertion and kill the app. The shell clears the flag at the start of each engine frame.
+static bool v_frame_rendered;
+bool V_FrameRendered(bool clear)
+{
+    bool r = v_frame_rendered;
+    if (clear)
+        v_frame_rendered = false;
+    return r;
+}
+
 //=============
 
 static cvar_t   *cl_add_particles;
@@ -660,6 +674,7 @@
     }
 
     R_RenderFrame(&cl.refdef);
+    v_frame_rendered = true;   // [stereo overlay] a second-eye render is now safe this frame
 #if USE_DEBUG
     if (cl_stats->integer)
         Com_Printf("ent:%i  lt:%i  part:%i\n", r_numentities, r_numdlights, r_numparticles);
